# Observe Retributive Mirror reflecting one third of incoming damage back at the
# attacker, for bd inc-tek.8.7 (PA-07-F5).
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/retributive-mirror.keys 1
#
# WHAT IS MEASURED. Retributive Mirror is an EA_INFLICT self-buff whose
# META(PRE(EVICTIM(EV_DAMAGE))) handler throws `bonus = e.vDmg / N` back at any
# creature that strikes the warded caster (message source "retributive strike").
# The spell's own Desc promises "one third of all damage dealt to you (round
# down) is reflected", so N MUST be 3; the pre-fix line used 5. The reflected
# damage is applied silently -- it prints no combat line -- so the oracle reads
# it as the ATTACKER's hit-point drop, cross-checked against the incoming
# damages the log prints with "Show All Combat Rolls" on.
#
# WHY A FIRE GIANT. A fire giant (MA_GIANT, M_EVIL) is hostile the instant it is
# summoned and hits hard enough that its melee bypasses the caster's armour, so
# each incoming e.vDmg is large and floor(/3) and floor(/5) differ by a clear
# margin. Free Advancement raises the barbarian to level 5 for hit points, and
# Cheat Death guarantees he survives the giant's full attack routine so the
# giant's hit-point drop stays readable; the reflection has already struck the
# giant by the time any death is resolved.
#
# HOW TO READ IT. "Examine Nearby Things" starts on the player; RIGHT cycles to
# the next thing, and a monster's Dump prints its HP:cur/max. giant-before reads
# max/max; giant-after reads (max - reflected)/max. The reflected total equals
# the sum of floor(incoming_i / 3) over the giant's hits, read from the log.

@include chargen.keys

# One visit to the switches submenu. First wizard entry needs the "Enter wizard
# mode? [yn]" confirm (w y); later entries do not (w alone). Rows top-to-bottom:
# 1 Cheat Death, 3 Free Advancement, 12 Show All Combat Rolls.
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
SPACE
DOWN*2
SPACE
DOWN*9
SPACE
ESC

# Raise the barbarian to level 5 for survivable hit points.
d
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
ESC

# Make Retributive Mirror castable regardless of class.
w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Retributive Mirror"
ENTER

# Summon a fire giant one square east of the caster.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Giant"
@choose "fire giant"
RIGHT
ENTER

# Read the giant's hit points before any blow lands (max/max).
w
@choose "Examine Nearby Things"
@until "'H'" RIGHT
@dump:giant-before
ESC

# Cast Retributive Mirror on the caster himself. "*" targets self.
m
@choose "Retributive Mirror"
*

# Let the giant take one turn and strike. Cheat Death revives the caster if the
# routine would kill him; the reflection has already struck the giant.
.
@while "Die?" y

# Read the giant's hit points after the blows (max - reflected)/max.
w
@choose "Examine Nearby Things"
@until "'H'" RIGHT
@dump:giant-after
ESC

# The combat log: every incoming damage number, for the floor(inc/3) cross-check.
v
@dump:log0
PGUP
@dump:log1
@while "Messages" ESC
@quit
